    "body": "**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nWhen the Chatwoot widget is loaded it sets a cookie `cw_conversation`. It seems like this is uneccessary, and is only ever needed if the vistor interacts with the widget.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\nLoad the chat widget script on a webpage.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nThe widget should only set a cookie after the visitor opens/interacts with it as that's when the conversation starts.\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n\r\nIf applicable, add screenshots to help explain your problem.\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1462828/112114759-61db2e00-8bf3-11eb-8355-a9738e37afa2.png)\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n\r\nBoth environments. \r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nMy company is anti-tracking so don't wish to use any tracking cookies. This cookie is used for tracking and would require us to show a cookie banner.",
